          "meeting_id": "57F042",
          "quote": "First, the section headers in the PDF export are getting cut off."
        },
        {
          "meeting_id": "C9E300",
          "quote": "Like, if you've got a tenant with over, um, I think it was around 50,000 audit log entries in the window, the report generation was timing out."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Contract Renewal and Expansion",
      "definition": "Calls discussing scheduled contract renewals, seat expansion terms, multi-year commitments, and cross-selling additional platform modules.",
      "distinguishing": "Differs from churn retention saves by focusing on healthy accounts seeking proactive expansions, module additions, or multi-year cost structures.",
      "owner": "sales / account manager",
      "actionable_because": "An account manager would generate renewal quotes, structure multi-year term discounts, and bundle modules like Identity or Detect.",
      "meeting_ids": ["2AA9F5", "30237B", "39CFC7", "99EE7D", "E7A00D"],
      "evidence": [
        {
          "meeting_id": "2AA9F5",
          "quote": "Your current contract is up at the end of April, and we've put together a renewal proposal that keeps your Protect and Comply licensing at the same rate with a three-year lock, and then we've got a bundle option that folds in Detect at a meaningful discount if you want to explore that after the demo."
        },
        {
          "meeting_id": "39CFC7",
          "quote": "If you're willing to go to a two-year term, I can probably bring that number down closer to where you are now."
        },
        {
          "meeting_id": "99EE7D",
          "quote": "We can structure this as an elastic seat model where you have a committed baseline but you can flex up without triggering a full contract renegotiation, and we true-up annually."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Detect Tuning and Noise Optimization",
      "definition": "Calls focused on configuring behavioral baselines, suppressing false-positive spikes, and tuning detection thresholds to prevent alert fatigue.",
      "distinguishing": "Differs from outage discussions by addressing the accuracy, sensitivity, and operational noise of alerts during normal system operation.",
      "owner": "support lead",
      "actionable_because": "A support lead would supply baseline restoration workflows, craft tailored alert suppression guidelines, and escalate baseline engine resets to engineering.",
      "meeting_ids": ["657CF1", "A8C495"],
      "evidence": [
        {
          "meeting_id": "657CF1",
          "quote": "Saturday morning I come in and my dashboard is just... lit up. Hundreds of critical alerts."
        },
        {
          "meeting_id": "657CF1",
          "quote": "First, I can push a configuration update to manually restore your previous baseline snapshot — we keep a 30-day history of your tuning profiles, so we can roll back to where you were before the patch."
        },
        {
          "meeting_id": "A8C495",
          "quote": "Aegis Detect has baseline learning built in — it runs in observation mode for the first seven days and builds a behavioral baseline before it starts generating production alerts."
        }
      ]
